A||N||9||burdell1||Major oil leakage!||||5||
Z||000000||burdell1||05-05-2000||11:09 AM||||I am having trouble with my '85 2.8L V6. I am having some major oil leakage. I have to put a half quart in (at least) every other day. There is smoke coming from the back of the car--through the rear air vents (it comes out blue when first starting then it is white). The smoke is so harsh it actually leaves a white film on the back window....it also stalls when coming to a stop after i have been driving at high rates of speed. it also leaks below the car as well. it stalls upon start up as well. The check engine light has come on a couple of times, but i haven't had a chance to check it yet....any ideas????||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||05-05-2000||11:36 AM||||I have a few ideas. rings, guides, valves, gaskets, heads, block, rr main oil seal, etc. Sounds like you will most likely need a major overhaul, IF the main components(block, heads, etc) are still useable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||05-05-2000||12:06 PM||||Before tearing the whole engine down, replace the distributor O-ring and the valve cover gaskets (get the fel-pro high performance rubber ones).<P>After that, make sure the engine is cleaned up (so no oil is burning off the block) and see if it still smokes.  After that, check your compression and monitor your oil consumption.  If it still leaks, then you may be looking at rear main seal, oil pan, blow by, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||burdell1||05-05-2000||12:09 PM||||It does have blow by but what does that mean engine-wise? is she a goner?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||05-05-2000||01:27 PM||||I would also check oil for water(oil looks milky), and water for oil. If either condition is present, the valve cover gaskets and dist. o-ring will do no good. <P>Remember, the gaskets mentioned in the previous post will only rememdy the oil burning if those are the culprits. They will do nothing about the coolant filming up the outside of the rear glass. First, I would do a comp. check on ALL cylinders, not just the 3 easiest to reach. Then, find out where all this coolant is coming from, if you're lucky, it will just be a bad hose or connection. Then, track down all oil leaks. Clean up the entire engine and tranny. This will help eliminate some of the buring oil and coolant, so you can get a better idea of where the liquids are coming from. After these are adressed, it might be easier to track down the stall conditions.||||reg||1
Z||000005||burdell1||05-05-2000||01:42 PM||||the burning smoke i assume is from the oil, and not the coolant. I do not think it is burning coolant at all.||||reg||1
Z||000006||burdell1||05-05-2000||02:20 PM||||the codes that came up were 32 and 35.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mshill||05-05-2000||03:02 PM||||burdell1, blowby means at the very least the rings are shot.  Fiero56 is correct about oil in water and vice-versa.  That is head gasket, cracked head or cracked block.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Haze_Performance||05-05-2000||05:03 PM||||Its not looking good. Time for a rebuild.||||reg||8
Z||000009||burdell1||05-05-2000||07:21 PM||||It doesn't seem to have any oil in the coolant or vice versa...||||reg||1
